#: ../../../advanced/warp-level-programming.md:57
msgid ""
"All shuffles are **warp-synchronous** — they implicitly synchronize the "
"warp. No `sync_threads()` is needed, and in fact calling `sync_threads()` "
"inside a shuffle pattern would be both unnecessary and wasteful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/warp-level-programming.md:63
msgid "Warp reduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/warp-level-programming.md:65
msgid ""
"The most common shuffle pattern is a **butterfly reduction**: in ⌈log₂(32)⌉ "
"= 5 steps, every lane accumulates the sum (or min, max, etc.) of all 32 "
"values. No shared memory, no barriers, five shuffle steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/warp-level-programming.md:73
msgid ""
"Butterfly reduction using `shuffle_xor`. At each step, lanes exchange values "
"with their XOR partner and add. After 5 steps (masks 16, 8, 4, 2, 1), lane 0 "
"holds the sum of all 32 values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/warp-level-programming.md:78
msgid ""
"use cuda_device::warp;\n"
"\n"
"fn warp_reduce_sum(mut val: f32) -> f32 {\n"
"    val += warp::shuffle_xor_f32(val, 16);\n"
"    val += warp::shuffle_xor_f32(val, 8);\n"
"    val += warp::shuffle_xor_f32(val, 4);\n"
"    val += warp::shuffle_xor_f32(val, 2);\n"
"    val += warp::shuffle_xor_f32(val, 1);\n"
"    val\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/warp-level-programming.md:91
msgid ""
"After the reduction, **all 32 lanes** hold the sum (because XOR is symmetric "
"— both partners accumulate). If you only need the result in lane 0, you can "
"use `shuffle_down` instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/warp-level-programming.md:95
msgid ""
"fn warp_reduce_sum_lane0(mut val: f32) -> f32 {\n"
"    val += warp::shuffle_down_f32(val, 16);\n"
"    val += warp::shuffle_down_f32(val, 8);\n"
"    val += warp::shuffle_down_f32(val, 4);\n"
"    val += warp::shuffle_down_f32(val, 2);\n"
"    val += warp::shuffle_down_f32(val, 1);\n"
"    val\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/warp-level-programming.md:106
msgid ""
"With `shuffle_down`, only lane 0 holds the correct result — the others hold "
"partial sums. This is fine when only lane 0 writes the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/warp-level-programming.md:110
msgid ""
"Need a block-wide reduction? Reduce within each warp using shuffles, write "
"the 32 per-warp results to shared memory, `sync_threads()`, then reduce the "
"warp-level results with one final warp. This hybrid approach is faster than "
"a pure shared memory tree because it eliminates 5 levels of barriers."
msgstr ""

